A||N||5||84fieroman||Turn signal not working||||8||
Z||000000||84fieroman||07-09-2001||07:46 AM||||Have problem with right turn signal not working on 84 SE.  When try to turn on can hear clicking coming from dash but arrow indicator light on dash doesn't work nor any of the outside indicators blink.  Have changed all bulbs to new but didn't help.  Also, not sure if related but can't use emergency flashers because when turn those on fuse blows.  Any ideas???  <p>[This message has been edited by 84fieroman (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||07-09-2001||01:48 PM||||sounds like you definetly have a electrical short.ther is no easy solution to this problem.you will need to look for a wire rubbing touching on metal.this is time consuming.goodluck||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||07-09-2001||07:27 PM||||start looking for the bare or shorted wire under the front fender and bumper near the lite assembly. the turn sig in also connected to front side marker lites, so check that too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||84fieroman||07-10-2001||07:45 AM||||Looked at all of that and it seems O.K.  Don't know if this has anything to do with it but fuse blows (20 amp)  when brakes applied and when emergency flashers turned on.  I think related to the right turn signal problem some how.  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>start looking for the bare or shorted wire under the front fender and bumper near the lite assembly. the turn sig in also connected to front side marker lites, so check that too.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
